      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Use "
        },
        {
          "type": "strong",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Add Cards from Map"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " in the top-right toolbar, then select"
        },
        {
          "type": "strong",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " Coordinate"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ". The Add Points editor opens beside the map toolbar. Add one or several points, edit each row's latitude and longitude, and choose its marker icon."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "add-single-point-003",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Step 1: Start the Shortcut"
        }
      ],
      "role": "feature-title"
    },
    {
      "id": "add-single-point-004",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Click the pencil-shaped "
        },
        {
          "type": "strong",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Add Card from Map"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " button, then choose"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        },
        {
          "type": "strong",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Coordinate"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ". Add Points opens directly to the left of the toolbar."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "add-single-point-005",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Step 2: Add and Refine Points"
        }
      ],
      "role": "feature-title"
    },
    {
      "id": "add-single-point-006",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Use the plus tool and click the map to add points. Edit coordinates in the numbered rows, change icons, or remove individual points. New markers have a dark outline and translucent gray fill; saved custom colors are preserved. The toolbar provides color, opacity, move, rotate, scale, undo, redo, and clear controls. Unavailable actions are disabled."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "add-single-point-007",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Step 3: Complete Project Data"
        }
      ],
      "role": "feature-title"
    },
    {
      "id": "add-single-point-008",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Click Save to transfer points into the Project Creation form, then fill title, category, description, links, images, files, and optional ArcGIS links. Submit to create a point-based project marker on the map. Saving points alone does not create a project. Cancel leaves the map editor without applying changes."
        }
      ]
    }
